    "narrative": "**Mickey Moniak** is the clear anchor for Ghost Ride the WHIP today, headlining our lineup with a 75.75 efficiency score. His matchup against Gusto is a perfect storm of environmental and situational upside, benefiting from a 14% park factor boost and the opposing pitcher\u2019s notoriously slow delivery, which significantly improves his stolen base equity. We are also leaning heavily on **Josh Naylor** (65.22) in the 5-hole against Ure\u00f1a; his ability to capitalize on a favorable 4.40 xERA matchup makes him our most reliable source for RBI production today. While **Dalton Rushing** falls into the marginal bucket, his elite hold SP metrics and a wind-aided environment keep him in the starting nine despite a suppressed spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Zach McKinstry**, whose 36.27 score landed him just below our \"Zebras\" floor of 40.0. While his profile typically provides useful utility, he is being stifled by a difficult matchup against Eovaldi and a suboptimal #7 batting order slot. We are playing it safe to preserve our game cap, as the 3.42 xERA of the opposing starter provides no relief for a player whose base projection is already trending downward. Conversely, we remain in a holding pattern regarding our elite stolen base threats, as **Corbin Carroll** is out of action today and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains sidelined on the IL. We will continue to monitor **Edwin Arroyo** and **James Wood** for future shifts in platoon advantages, but for today, the current configuration offers the optimal risk-adjusted path to maintaining our edge in the 5x5 categories.",
